{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T13:15:34.288115", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # First, check if the primitive is already in the inventory\n  # If so, return empty action list (no actions needed)\n  if env._current_state.inventory[env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]] > 0:\n      return []\n  \n  # Check if there are any items that can be crafted to get the primitive\n  # For now, let's assume we only want to collect primitives, not craft them\n  # So we'll check if the primitive is in environment or grabbable_indices\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # If primitive is not in grabbable indices, then it's not directly collectable\n  if primitive_index not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return []  # Cannot collect this primitive\n\n  # Try to find the primitive using a simple BFS-like approach\n  visited = set()\n  queue = collections.deque([(env._current_state.pos, [])])\n  visited.add(env._current_state.pos)\n  \n  while queue:\n      pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      \n      # Check if we've found the primitive at this position\n      if env._current_state.grid[pos[0], pos[1], primitive_index] > 0:\n          return path\n      \n      # Get neighbors (up, down, left, right)\n      for dx, dy in [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]:\n          new_pos = (pos[0] + dx, pos[1] + dy)\n          \n          # Check bounds\n          if (new_pos[0] < 0 or new_pos[0] >= env.world.cookbook.n_kinds or \n              new_pos[1] < 0 or new_pos[1] >= env.world.cookbook.n_kinds):\n              continue\n          \n          # Check if we can move to this position (not blocked by environment)\n          # For simplicity, let's assume we can move through any non-environment cell\n          if new_pos not in visited:\n              # If the primitive is here, return the path\n              if env._current_state.grid[new_pos[0], new_pos[1], primitive_index] > 0:\n                  return path + [env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]]\n              \n              # Otherwise, add to queue for further exploration\n              visited.add(new_pos)\n              queue.append((new_pos, path + [0]))  # Placeholder action\n  \n  return []  # No path found", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
