{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T13:21:42.325732", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Initialize variables\n  action_list = [] \n  reward = 0\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # Check if primitive is already in inventory\n  prim_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if state.inventory[prim_index] > 0:\n      return state, reward, action_list\n\n  # If not, find the closest location of the primitive\n  # This is a simplified approach; a more sophisticated one would use pathfinding algorithms\n  grid = state.grid\n  pos = state.pos\n  height, width, n_kinds = grid.shape\n\n  # Find all positions with the primitive\n  primitive_positions = []\n  for x in range(width):\n      for y in range(height):\n          if grid[y, x, prim_index] > 0:\n              primitive_positions.append((x, y))\n\n  if not primitive_positions:\n      # Primitive not found in the environment\n      return state, reward, action_list\n\n  # Find the closest primitive position to the agent's current position\n  min_distance = float('inf')\n  closest_pos = None\n  for px, py in primitive_positions:\n      distance = abs(px - pos[0]) + abs(py - pos[1])  # Manhattan distance\n      if distance < min_distance:\n          min_distance = distance\n          closest_pos = (px, py)\n\n  if closest_pos is None:\n      return state, reward, action_list\n\n  # Plan movement to the closest primitive\n  target_x, target_y = closest_pos\n  agent_x, agent_y = pos\n\n  # Move towards the primitive\n  while (agent_x, agent_y) != (target_x, target_y):\n      if agent_x < target_x:\n          action_list.append(3)  # RIGHT\n          agent_x += 1\n      elif agent_x > target_x:\n          action_list.append(2)  # LEFT\n          agent_x -= 1\n      elif agent_y < target_y:\n          action_list.append(0)  # DOWN\n          agent_y += 1\n      elif agent_y > target_y:\n          action_list.append(1)  # UP\n          agent_y -= 1\n\n  # Add the pickup action at the final position\n  if (agent_x, agent_y) == (target_x, target_y):\n      action_list.append(4)  # USE to collect the primitive\n\n  # Execute actions\n  for a in action_list:\n      r, state = env.step(state, a)\n      reward += r\n\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 4, "scores": {"3": -1}}
