{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T13:21:50.877553", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # TODO: Implement this function\n  # You are allowed to use any functions from the code base, but you must not use any other libraries or imports.\n  # You can use numpy.random, time, collections and env_factory.\n  # The solution should be a sequence of actions that collect the specified primitive.\n\n  # Hint:\n  # - Use env._current_state.features_dict() to get the current state features.\n  # - Use env.step(action) to execute an action and get the next state.\n  # - Use env.observation() to get the current observation.\n  # - You can access the inventory using env._current_state.inventory.\n  # - You can access the grid using env._current_state.grid.\n  # - You can access the position using env._current_state.pos.\n  # - You can access the direction using env._current_state.dir.\n\n  action_list = [] \n  reward = 0\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # Check if the primitive is already in inventory\n  if state.inventory[env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]] > 0:\n    return state, reward, action_list\n\n  # Check if the primitive is available in the grid\n  pos = state.pos\n  grid = state.grid\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # If the primitive is at the current position\n  if grid[pos[0], pos[1], primitive_index] > 0:\n    action_list.append(4)  # USE action to collect\n    return state, reward, action_list\n\n  # TODO: Implement pathfinding to reach the primitive\n  # For now, we just return an empty list as a placeholder\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 9, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
