{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T13:35:54.853047", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Get the index for the primitive\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Get current position and inventory\n  pos = state.pos\n  inventory = state.inventory\n\n  # Check if primitive is already in inventory\n  if inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return state, reward, action_list\n\n  # Find nearby cells with the primitive\n  # This is a simplified approach - in practice, you'd need to implement pathfinding\n  found = False\n  for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n      for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n          x, y = pos[0] + dx, pos[1] + dy\n          if 0 <= x < env.world.WIDTH and 0 <= y < env.world.HEIGHT:\n              if state.grid[x, y, primitive_index] > 0:\n                  # Move to that cell (this is simplified)\n                  if dx == -1:\n                      action_list.append(2)  # LEFT\n                  elif dx == 1:\n                      action_list.append(3)  # RIGHT\n                  elif dy == -1:\n                      action_list.append(0)  # UP\n                  elif dy == 1:\n                      action_list.append(1)  # DOWN\n                  found = True\n                  break\n      if found:\n          break\n\n  # If we're at the primitive location, pick it up\n  if found and state.grid[pos[0], pos[1], primitive_index] > 0:\n      action_list.append(4)  # USE (pickup)\n\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
