{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T13:37:02.612037", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Get the index for the primitive\n  cookbook = env.world.cookbook\n  primitive_index = cookbook.index.get(primitive)\n  if primitive_index is None:\n      return [], 0, []\n  \n  # Check if already in inventory\n  if state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return [], 0, []\n\n  # Use a simple pathfinding algorithm to find the primitive\n  # This is a placeholder for actual pathfinding logic\n  # For now, we'll simulate a basic movement towards the primitive\n  pos = state.pos\n  grid = state.grid\n\n  # Find the nearest cell containing the primitive\n  min_dist = float('inf')\n  target_pos = None\n  for i in range(grid.shape[0]):\n      for j in range(grid.shape[1]):\n          if grid[i, j] == primitive_index:\n              dist = abs(i - pos[0]) + abs(j - pos[1])\n              if dist < min_dist:\n                  min_dist = dist\n                  target_pos = (i, j)\n\n  # If no primitive found, return empty actions\n  if target_pos is None:\n      return [], 0, []\n\n  action_list = []\n  current_pos = pos\n\n  while current_pos != target_pos:\n      # Move towards the target\n      if current_pos[0] < target_pos[0]:\n          action_list.append(1)  # UP\n          current_pos = (current_pos[0] + 1, current_pos[1])\n      elif current_pos[0] > target_pos[0]:\n          action_list.append(0)  # DOWN\n          current_pos = (current_pos[0] - 1, current_pos[1])\n      elif current_pos[1] < target_pos[1]:\n          action_list.append(3)  # RIGHT\n          current_pos = (current_pos[0], current_pos[1] + 1)\n      elif current_pos[1] > target_pos[1]:\n          action_list.append(2)  # LEFT\n          current_pos = (current_pos[0], current_pos[1] - 1)\n\n  # Add the pickup action\n  action_list.append(4)  # USE\n\n  reward = 0\n  for a in action_list:\n      r, state = env.step(state, a)\n      reward += r\n\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
