{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T13:37:20.661996", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # We need to implement this function\n  # First we get the index of the primitive from the environment\n  # Then we check if it's in our inventory\n  # If not, we need to move towards it and collect it\n\n  action_list = []\n  reward = 0\n  state = env._current_state\n  # Get the index of the primitive\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Check if we already have it in our inventory\n  if state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return state, reward, action_list\n\n  # Otherwise, we need to find and collect it\n  # This is a simple implementation - we'll just move around until we find it\n  # In a real implementation, we'd want to use pathfinding\n  found = False\n  while not found:\n      # Check if the primitive is in the current view\n      for i in range(3):  # 3x3 neighborhood\n          for j in range(3):\n              pos = (state.pos[0] + i - 1, state.pos[1] + j - 1)\n              if pos[0] >= 0 and pos[0] < env.world.WIDTH and pos[1] >= 0 and pos[1] < env.world.HEIGHT:\n                  if state.grid[pos[0], pos[1], primitive_index] > 0:\n                      # Found it, move to collect\n                      if i == 1 and j == 1:\n                          # Already at the position, use to collect\n                          action_list.append(4)  # USE action\n                          found = True\n                          break\n                      else:\n                          # Move towards it\n                          if i < 1:\n                              action_list.append(2)  # LEFT\n                          elif i > 1:\n                              action_list.append(3)  # RIGHT\n                          if j < 1:\n                              action_list.append(0)  # UP\n                          elif j > 1:\n                              action_list.append(1)  # DOWN\n                          found = True\n                          break\n      if not found:\n          # If we can't find it, move randomly or try to use a tool\n          # This is a placeholder - in practice, we'd implement proper pathfinding\n          action_list.append(0)  # UP\n          \n  for a in action_list:\n      r, state = env.step(state, a)\n      reward += r\n\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
