{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T13:51:04.855339", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Get the index for the target primitive\n  if primitive not in env.world.cookbook.index.contents:\n      raise ValueError(f\"Unknown primitive: {primitive}\")\n\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Check if we already have this primitive\n  if state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return [], 0, []\n\n  # Use the existing collect logic from craft.py\n  # This function should be implemented to handle the actual collection\n  # For now, let's create a placeholder implementation\n  actions = []\n  \n  # If primitive is not in inventory, we need to move towards it\n  # Find the primitive in the grid and generate path\n  found = False\n  for y in range(state.grid.shape[1]):\n      for x in range(state.grid.shape[0]):\n          if state.grid[x, y, primitive_index] > 0:\n              # Found the primitive\n              found = True\n              # Calculate distance to reach it\n              dx = x - state.pos[0]\n              dy = y - state.pos[1]\n              \n              # Generate actions to move towards the primitive\n              while dx != 0 or dy != 0:\n                  if dx > 0:\n                      actions.append(3)  # RIGHT\n                      dx -= 1\n                  elif dx < 0:\n                      actions.append(2)  # LEFT\n                      dx += 1\n                  elif dy > 0:\n                      actions.append(1)  # UP\n                      dy -= 1\n                  elif dy < 0:\n                      actions.append(0)  # DOWN\n                      dy += 1\n              \n              # Pick it up with USE action\n              actions.append(4)  # USE\n              break\n      if found:\n          break\n\n  return state, reward, actions", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
