{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T14:08:11.076959", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # The following is just an example to show the usage of the DSL constructs\n  # You should replace this with your own implementation\n\n  def get_primitive_index(primitive: str):\n      # Get the index of the primitive in the environment\n      return env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  def can_reach_primitive(state, primitive_index):\n      # Check if the agent can reach the primitive given its current inventory\n      return state.next_to(primitive_index)\n\n  def get_action_to_primitive(state, primitive_index):\n      # Get action to move towards the primitive\n      return env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  primitive_index = get_primitive_index(primitive)\n  if not can_reach_primitive(state, primitive_index):\n    # Implement pathfinding logic here\n    pass\n\n  action_list = []\n  reward = 0\n  for a in action_list:\n      r, state = env.step(state, a)\n      reward += r\n\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
