{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T14:09:52.804049", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # We use the following helper functions to identify relevant entities\n  # and determine their positions in the grid.\n  def get_entity_positions(entity_index):\n      \"\"\"Return a list of (row, col) positions where entity_index occurs.\"\"\"\n      positions = []\n      for r in range(env.world.scenario.init_grid.shape[0]):\n          for c in range(env.world.scenario.init_grid.shape[1]):\n              if env.world.scenario.init_grid[r, c, entity_index] > 0:\n                  positions.append((r, c))\n      return positions\n\n  def get_agent_position():\n      \"\"\"Return current agent position (row, col).\"\"\"\n      return state.pos\n\n  def manhattan_distance(pos1, pos2):\n      \"\"\"Compute Manhattan distance between two positions.\"\"\"\n      return abs(pos1[0] - pos2[0]) + abs(pos1[1] - pos2[1])\n\n  # Identify the primitive index\n  prim_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Get all possible locations of this primitive in the grid\n  prim_positions = get_entity_positions(prim_index)\n  \n  if not prim_positions:\n      # Primitive not found, return empty action list\n      return state, reward, action_list\n\n  # Find the closest primitive location\n  agent_pos = get_agent_position()\n  closest_pos = min(prim_positions, key=lambda p: manhattan_distance(agent_pos, p))\n  \n  # Simple pathfinding logic:\n  # For now, we just use basic moves toward the closest position.\n  # More sophisticated pathfinding could be implemented here.\n\n  # Generate a simple sequence of moves to approach the primitive\n  action_list = []\n  current_pos = agent_pos\n  \n  while current_pos != closest_pos:\n      dr = closest_pos[0] - current_pos[0]\n      dc = closest_pos[1] - current_pos[1]\n      \n      if abs(dr) > abs(dc):\n          # Move vertically first\n          if dr > 0:\n              action_list.append(1)  # UP\n          else:\n              action_list.append(0)  # DOWN\n          current_pos = (current_pos[0] + (1 if dr > 0 else -1), current_pos[1])\n      else:\n          # Move horizontally first\n          if dc > 0:\n              action_list.append(3)  # RIGHT\n          else:\n              action_list.append(2)  # LEFT\n          current_pos = (current_pos[0], current_pos[1] + (1 if dc > 0 else -1))\n  \n  # Add a final pickup action (if applicable)\n  # In this simple implementation, we assume the primitive is directly reachable.\n  # For a full implementation, we'd need to check if there's an actual item at\n  # `closest_pos` and whether it can be picked up.\n\n  reward = 0\n  for a in action_list:\n      r, state = env.step(state, a)\n      reward += r\n\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
