{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T14:11:26.469952", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Find the index of the primitive in the environment\n  # Use BFS to find the shortest path to collect the primitive\n  # If the agent is already holding the primitive, return an empty list\n\n  action_list = [] \n  reward = 0\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # Check if the agent is already holding the primitive\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  if state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return state, reward, action_list\n\n  # Find the position of the primitive in the grid\n  pos = None\n  for i in range(state.grid.shape[0]):\n      for j in range(state.grid.shape[1]):\n          if state.grid[i][j][primitive_index] == 1:\n              pos = (i, j)\n              break\n\n  # If the primitive is not found, return an empty list\n  if pos is None:\n      return state, reward, action_list\n\n  # Use BFS to find the shortest path to collect the primitive\n  queue = collections.deque([(state.pos, [])])\n  visited = set()\n  visited.add(state.pos)\n\n  while queue:\n      current_pos, path = queue.popleft()\n      \n      if current_pos == pos:\n          # Found the path, return it\n          return state, reward, path\n      \n      # Explore neighbors\n      for direction in [0, 1, 2, 3]:  # UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT\n          new_pos = env.world._move(current_pos, direction)\n          \n          if new_pos in visited:\n              continue\n          \n          # Check if the move is valid (not out of bounds and not an obstacle)\n          if (0 <= new_pos[0] < state.grid.shape[0] and \n              0 <= new_pos[1] < state.grid.shape[1] and\n              state.grid[new_pos[0]][new_pos[1]][env.world.water_index] == 0):\n              \n              visited.add(new_pos)\n              queue.append((new_pos, path + [direction]))\n\n  # If no path is found, return an empty list\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 4, "scores": 