{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T14:21:23.525588", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Initialize action list and tracking variables\n  action_list = [] \n  reward = 0\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # Get the index for the target primitive\n  prim_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # If the primitive is already in inventory, we're done\n  if state.inventory[prim_index] > 0:\n      return state, reward, action_list\n\n  # Define a helper function to get the next action\n  def get_next_action(target_pos):\n      pos = state.pos\n      if target_pos[0] < pos[0]:\n          return craft.LEFT\n      elif target_pos[0] > pos[0]:\n          return craft.RIGHT\n      elif target_pos[1] < pos[1]:\n          return craft.UP\n      elif target_pos[1] > pos[1]:\n          return craft.DOWN\n      else:\n          return None  # Already at the target position\n\n  # Find all positions of the primitive in the grid\n  primitive_positions = []\n  for i in range(state.grid.shape[0]):\n      for j in range(state.grid.shape[1]):\n          if state.grid[i, j, prim_index] > 0:\n              primitive_positions.append((i, j))\n\n  # If no positions found, return an empty action list (no path)\n  if not primitive_positions:\n      return state, reward, action_list\n\n  # Choose the closest position\n  closest_pos = primitive_positions[0]\n  min_distance = abs(closest_pos[0] - state.pos[0]) + abs(closest_pos[1] - state.pos[1])\n  for pos in primitive_positions:\n      distance = abs(pos[0] - state.pos[0]) + abs(pos[1] - state.pos[1])\n      if distance < min_distance:\n          min_distance = distance\n          closest_pos = pos\n\n  # Move towards the primitive position\n  while state.pos != closest_pos:\n      action = get_next_action(closest_pos)\n      if action is not None:\n          r, state = env.step(state, action)\n          reward += r\n          action_list.append(action)\n      else:\n          break  # Should not happen if we're correctly calculating the path\n\n  # At this point, the agent should be at the primitive's position.\n  # If it's not in inventory, there may be an obstacle or a need to craft a tool.\n  # For now, assume we can directly collect it (i.e., it's a grabbable item).\n  if state.inventory[prim_index] == 0:\n      # Try to use any tools that might help in collecting this primitive\n      # For example, using a bridge to cross water or a pickaxe to mine gems\n      # This is a simplified approach - in reality, more complex logic would be needed.\n      \n      # Let's see if we can directly move there and collect it (assuming it's a grabbable item)\n      pass  # Placeholder for more advanced tool usage logic\n\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
