{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T14:24:00.879582", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # TODO: Implement the function here.\n  # You may use any of the functions in the code base as well as the classes.\n  # The function should return a list of actions to collect the specified primitive.\n  # The function should not craft or use any tools.\n  # The function should not try to collect primitives that are not passed as the argument.\n  # The function should return an empty list if the primitive is already in the inventory.\n  # The function should return an empty list if the primitive is not reachable.\n  # The function should return a sequence of actions that leads to collecting the primitive.\n  # The function should be able to handle any primitive that is in the environment.\n\n  action_list = [] \n  reward = 0\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # If the primitive is already in the inventory, return empty list\n  if state.inventory[state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]] > 0:\n      return action_list\n\n  # If the primitive is not reachable, return empty list\n  if primitive not in state.world.cookbook.index:\n      return action_list\n\n  # Try to find a path to collect the primitive\n  primitive_index = state.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  current_pos = state.pos\n  target_pos = None\n\n  # Find the position of the primitive in the grid\n  for i in range(state.grid.shape[0]):\n      for j in range(state.grid.shape[1]):\n          if state.grid[i, j, primitive_index] == 1:\n              target_pos = (i, j)\n              break\n      if target_pos:\n          break\n\n  # If the primitive is not found in the grid, return empty list\n  if not target_pos:\n      return action_list\n\n  # Simple path finding: move towards the target position\n  while current_pos != target_pos:\n      # Move horizontally first\n      if current_pos[1] < target_pos[1]:\n          action_list.append(3)  # RIGHT\n          current_pos = (current_pos[0], current_pos[1] + 1)\n      elif current_pos[1] > target_pos[1]:\n          action_list.append(2)  # LEFT\n          current_pos = (current_pos[0], current_pos[1] - 1)\n      # Move vertically if needed\n      elif current_pos[0] < target_pos[0]:\n          action_list.append(1)  # DOWN\n          current_pos = (current_pos[0] + 1, current_pos[1])\n      elif current_pos[0] > target_pos[0]:\n          action_list.append(0)  # UP\n          current_pos = (current_pos[0] - 1, current_pos[1])\n\n  # Add the pickup action at the end\n  action_list.append(4)  # USE\n\n  # Execute the actions to update state and reward\n  for a in action_list:\n      r, state = env.step(state, a)\n      reward += r\n\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
