{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T14:27:24.060994", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Get the index for the primitive\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # If we already have it, return empty action list\n  if state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return [], 0.0, []\n      \n  # If primitive is not grabbable (e.g., water, boundary), return failure\n  if primitive_index not in env.world.grabbable_indices:\n      return [], -1.0, []\n\n  # Find all cells with the primitive\n  primitive_cells = []\n  for x in range(env.world.WIDTH):\n      for y in range(env.world.HEIGHT):\n          if state.grid[x, y, primitive_index] > 0:\n              primitive_cells.append((x, y))\n  \n  # If we can't find it, try to craft it first\n  # TODO: Implement crafting logic here\n  \n  # If no cells found, return failure\n  if not primitive_cells:\n      return [], -1.0, []\n      \n  # Find the closest cell\n  pos = state.pos\n  closest_cell = min(primitive_cells, key=lambda p: abs(p[0] - pos[0]) + abs(p[1] - pos[1]))\n  \n  # Compute path to the cell\n  actions = compute_path_to(env, state, closest_cell)\n  if not actions:\n      return [], -1.0, []\n      \n  action_list.extend(actions)\n\n  # Add pickup action\n  action_list.append(craft.USE)  # Use to pick up\n\n  # Execute the actions\n  for a in action_list:\n      r, state = env.step(state, a)\n      reward += r\n\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 5, "scores": {"3": -1}}
