{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T14:31:18.941307", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Get the index of the primitive\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Check if we already have it\n  if state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return state, reward, action_list\n\n  # Find where the primitive is located\n  locations = []\n  for i in range(state.grid.shape[0]):\n      for j in range(state.grid.shape[1]):\n          if state.grid[i][j][primitive_index] == 1:\n              locations.append((i, j))\n  \n  # If we found it, move to it\n  if locations:\n      target = locations[0]\n      actions = []\n      while state.pos != target:\n          if state.pos[0] < target[0]:\n              actions.append(3)  # RIGHT\n          elif state.pos[0] > target[0]:\n              actions.append(2)  # LEFT\n          elif state.pos[1] < target[1]:\n              actions.append(1)  # DOWN\n          elif state.pos[1] > target[1]:\n              actions.append(0)  # UP\n          r, state = env.step(state, actions[-1])\n          reward += r\n      actions.append(4)  # USE to collect\n      r, state = env.step(state, actions[-1])\n      reward += r\n      return state, reward, actions\n\n  # If we can't find it, we need to craft or find a way to get there\n  # For now, let's assume we have the necessary tools or can use existing ones\n  # This is a simplified version - in practice you'd want more sophisticated pathfinding\n  \n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 3, "scores": {"3": -1}}
