{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T14:33:04.223428", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # If primitive is already in inventory, return empty action list\n  if state.inventory[env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]] > 0:\n      return [], 0.0, []\n\n  # Find the position of the primitive in the grid\n  prim_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  pos = np.where(state.grid[:, :, prim_index] == 1)\n  \n  if len(pos[0]) == 0:\n      # Primitive not found in grid\n      return [], -1.0, []\n\n  # Find path to primitive using BFS or similar algorithm\n  # For now, we assume a simple move towards the primitive position\n\n  # Placeholder for pathfinding logic\n  # This should be replaced with actual pathfinding code\n\n  # Simple heuristic: move towards the primitive if it's not adjacent\n  action_list = []\n  target_pos = (pos[0][0], pos[1][0])\n  agent_pos = state.pos\n\n  # Example logic to move toward target\n  if target_pos[0] > agent_pos[0]:\n      action_list.append(1)  # UP\n  elif target_pos[0] < agent_pos[0]:\n      action_list.append(0)  # DOWN\n  if target_pos[1] > agent_pos[1]:\n      action_list.append(3)  # RIGHT\n  elif target_pos[1] < agent_pos[1]:\n      action_list.append(2)  # LEFT\n\n  # If adjacent, add USE action to collect primitive\n  if abs(target_pos[0] - agent_pos[0]) <= 1 and abs(target_pos[1] - agent_pos[1]) <= 1:\n      action_list.append(4)  # USE\n\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": -1}}
