{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T14:39:42.213124", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # TODO: Implement this function.\n  # This function should compute a shortest path to reach and collect a given primitive (e.g., GOLD, GEM, WOOD) in the environment.\n  # It accounts for obstacles and environmental constraints by allowing the agent to use tools already in inventory\u2014\n  # for example:\n  #   - Using a BRIDGE to cross WATER in order to reach GOLD.\n  #   - Using a PICKAXE to mine GEM.\n\n  # The function assumes the world is static except for changes resulting from tool use (e.g., placing a bridge).\n  # It does not perform crafting or attempt to acquire new items\u2014only available tools in the inventory are used.\n\n  # Args:\n  #     env (env.CraftLab): The CraftLab environment instance.\n  #     primitive (str): The name of the primitive to collect.\n\n  # Returns:\n  #     List[int]: A list of action indices the agent can execute to collect the primitive.\n\n  pass", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T14:39:43.439513", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Initialize path tracking\n  visited = set()\n  queue = collections.deque([(state.pos, [], state)])  # (position, actions, state)\n  visited.add(state.pos)\n\n  # Define primitive indices and their properties\n  primitive_indices = env.world.cookbook.index.contents\n  primitive_index = primitive_indices[primitive]\n\n  # Check if primitive is already in inventory\n  if state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return [], 0.0, []\n\n  # Define movement actions\n  actions = [craft.DOWN, craft.UP, craft.LEFT, craft.RIGHT]\n  directions = [(1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]\n\n  while queue:\n      pos, path, current_state = queue.popleft()\n\n      # Check if the primitive is present at current position\n      if current_state.grid[pos[0], pos[1], primitive_index] > 0:\n          return path, 0.0, path\n\n      # Explore neighbors\n      for i, (dx, dy) in enumerate(directions):\n          new_pos = (pos[0] + dx, pos[1] + dy)\n          \n          # Check bounds and if already visited\n          if (new_pos[0] < 0 or new_pos[0] >= current_state.grid.shape[0] or \n              new_pos[1] < 0 or new_pos[1] >= current_state.grid.shape[1] or \n              new_pos in visited):\n              continue\n\n          # Check if the cell is passable (not a boundary or water unless we can cross it)\n          cell_content = current_state.grid[new_pos[0], new_pos[1]]\n          if cell_content[env.world.cookbook.index.contents['BOUNDARY']] > 0:\n              continue\n          \n          # If it's water, check if we can use a bridge or similar tool\n          if (cell_content[env.world.cookbook.index.contents['WATER']] > 0 and \n              not has_bridge_in_inventory(current_state)):\n              continue\n\n          # Move to new position and add to queue\n          visited.add(new_pos)\n          new_path = path + [actions[i]]\n          new_state = current_state.step(actions[i])\n          queue.append((new_pos, new_path, new_state))\n\n  # If no path found, return empty action list\n  return [], 0.0, []", "island_id": 2, "scores": {"3": -1}}
