{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T14:39:57.616516", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Get the index of the primitive we want to collect\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Get the current inventory\n  inventory = state.inventory\n\n  # If we already have it, return empty action list\n  if inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return [], 0, []\n\n  # Check if there is a direct path to collect this primitive\n  # This requires checking if any cell in the 3x3 neighborhood contains the primitive\n  pos = state.pos\n  grid = state.grid\n\n  # For each direction (up, down, left, right)\n  for dx, dy in [(0,1), (0,-1), (1,0), (-1,0)]:\n      nx, ny = pos[0] + dx, pos[1] + dy\n      if 0 <= nx < grid.shape[0] and 0 <= ny < grid.shape[1]:\n          # If the cell contains the primitive\n          if grid[nx, ny, primitive_index] > 0:\n              # Take the action to move into that cell (if not already there)\n              if pos == (nx, ny):\n                  return [], 0, []\n              else:\n                  # Determine which action to take\n                  if dx == 1:\n                      action = 3  # RIGHT\n                  elif dx == -1:\n                      action = 2  # LEFT\n                  elif dy == 1:\n                      action = 0  # DOWN\n                  else:  # dy == -1\n                      action = 1  # UP\n                  return [action], 0, [action]\n\n  # If no direct path, we need to check if we can craft a tool to reach it.\n  # For now, let's assume we can't and return an empty list (no actions possible)\n  return [], 0, []", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
