{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T14:40:37.256616", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Get the index of the primitive\n  idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Get the current state\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # Check if primitive is already in inventory\n  if state.inventory[idx] > 0:\n      return state, 0.0, []\n\n  # If we are already next to it, use the USE action\n  if state.next_to(idx):\n      # Use the USE action (assumed to be 4)\n      return state, 0.0, [4]\n\n  # Otherwise, move towards it\n  pos = state.pos\n  grid = state.grid\n\n  # Find the position of the primitive\n  found = False\n  target_pos = None\n  for i in range(grid.shape[0]):\n      for j in range(grid.shape[1]):\n          if grid[i, j, idx] > 0:\n              target_pos = (i, j)\n              found = True\n              break\n      if found:\n          break\n\n  # If we can't find it, return empty list\n  if not found:\n      return state, 0.0, []\n\n  # Move towards the primitive\n  action_list = []\n  while pos != target_pos:\n      i, j = pos\n      ti, tj = target_pos\n      if i < ti and grid[i+1, j, idx] > 0:\n          action_list.append(3)  # RIGHT\n          pos = (i+1, j)\n      elif i > ti and grid[i-1, j, idx] > 0:\n          action_list.append(2)  # LEFT\n          pos = (i-1, j)\n      elif j < tj and grid[i, j+1, idx] > 0:\n          action_list.append(1)  # DOWN\n          pos = (i, j+1)\n      elif j > tj and grid[i, j-1, idx] > 0:\n          action_list.append(0)  # UP\n          pos = (i, j-1)\n      else:\n          # If we can't move directly, try to find a path using BFS\n          break\n\n  return state, 0.0, action_list", "island_id": 8, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
