{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T14:57:07.846533", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Get the index of the primitive\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Check if we already have the primitive\n  if state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return state, reward, action_list\n\n  # Find the primitive in the environment using BFS\n  queue = collections.deque([(state.pos, 0)])\n  visited = set()\n  visited.add(state.pos)\n  \n  while queue:\n      pos, steps = queue.popleft()\n      \n      # If we found the primitive, collect it\n      if state.grid[pos[0], pos[1], primitive_index] > 0:\n          # Move to the position and pick up the item\n          actions_to_pos = get_actions_to_position(state.pos, pos)\n          action_list.extend(actions_to_pos)\n          \n          # Pick up the item\n          action_list.append(5)  # Assuming 5 is the pickup action\n          break\n      \n      # Explore neighbors\n      for dx, dy in [(0, 1), (1, 0), (0, -1), (-1, 0)]:\n          new_pos = (pos[0] + dx, pos[1] + dy)\n          \n          if (new_pos not in visited and \n              0 <= new_pos[0] < state.grid.shape[0] and \n              0 <= new_pos[1] < state.grid.shape[1]):\n              \n              visited.add(new_pos)\n              queue.append((new_pos, steps + 1))\n  \n  # If we have the primitive now, return\n  if state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return state, reward, action_list\n  \n  # Otherwise, use available tools to get it\n  # This part would need to be more complex to handle tool usage\n  \n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
