{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T15:08:24.307770", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # If we already have the primitive, no need to collect it.\n  if env._current_state.inventory[env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]] > 0:\n      return env._current_state, 0, []\n\n  action_list = [] \n  reward = 0\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # If we can directly pick up the primitive, do so.\n  if primitive in ['WOOD', 'STONE', 'IRON', 'GRASS', 'ROCK', 'GOLD', 'GEM']:\n      # Check if the primitive is directly accessible (e.g., on the ground).\n      for i in range(3):\n          for j in range(3):\n              if state.grid[state.pos[0]+i-1][state.pos[1]+j-1][env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]] > 0:\n                  # Move to that position and pick it up.\n                  action_list.append(env.action_specs()['DOWN'])\n                  break\n          else:\n              continue\n          break\n\n  # If we can't directly collect, check if we need to use tools.\n  # For example, to cross water to get gold, we might use a bridge.\n  if primitive == 'GOLD':\n      # Try to find a bridge in inventory.\n      bridge_index = env.world.cookbook.index['BRIDGE']\n      if state.inventory[bridge_index] > 0:\n          # Use the bridge (this would require implementing a USE action).\n          pass\n      # Check if we can go through water to get to gold.\n      # This requires more complex pathfinding.\n\n  # If primitive is not directly accessible, use pathfinding or crafting logic.\n  # Placeholder for pathfinding implementation.\n  # This part will be more complex and may require A* or BFS.\n\n  # For now, just return the state and actions as a placeholder.\n  for a in action_list:\n      r, state = env.step(state, a)\n      reward += r\n\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": 0.0}}
