{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T15:11:51.285138", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Initialize the CraftWorld and related components\n  world = env.world\n  cookbook = world.cookbook\n  index = cookbook.index\n\n  # Get the index for the primitive we want to collect\n  prim_index = index[primitive]\n\n  # If the primitive is not in the index, return empty action list\n  if prim_index is None:\n      return []\n\n  # Check if the primitive is already in the inventory\n  if state.inventory[prim_index] > 0:\n      return []\n\n  # Get the set of grabbable indices\n  grabbable_indices = world.grabbable_indices\n\n  # If the primitive is not grabbable, it might be a tool or something that can't be picked up\n  if prim_index not in grabbable_indices:\n      # Check if we have the required tools to get this item (e.g., bridge for water)\n      # For now, assume we can only collect items directly\n      return []\n\n  # If we reach here, it means we need to find and collect the primitive\n  # We'll use BFS to find the shortest path to the primitive\n  queue = collections.deque([(state.pos[0], state.pos[1], 0)])  # (x, y, steps)\n  visited = set()\n  visited.add(state.pos)\n\n  # Directions: UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT\n  directions = [(0, -1), (0, 1), (-1, 0), (1, 0)]\n\n  while queue:\n      x, y, steps = queue.popleft()\n\n      # Check if we found the primitive\n      if state.grid[x][y][prim_index] > 0:\n          # Found the primitive, now move to collect it\n          # Use a simple path to get there, assuming we can just walk to it\n          return action_list\n\n      # Explore neighbors\n      for dx, dy in directions:\n          nx, ny = x + dx, y + dy\n\n          # Check bounds and visited status\n          if 0 <= nx < state.grid.shape[0] and 0 <= ny < state.grid.shape[1]:\n              if (nx, ny) not in visited:\n                  # Check if the cell is walkable or contains the primitive\n                  if state.grid[nx][ny][prim_index] > 0 or state.grid[nx][ny][0] == 0:  # Assuming 0 means empty/walkable\n                      visited.add((nx, ny))\n                      queue.append((nx, ny, steps + 1))\n\n  # If we get here, we couldn't find a path to the primitive\n  return []", "island_id": 1, "scores": {"3": -1}}
