{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T15:14:32.914120", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # get the index of the primitive\n  primitive_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # if we already have it, return empty action list\n  if state.inventory[primitive_idx] > 0:\n      return [], 0.0, []\n\n  # otherwise, find a path to collect it\n  # This is a placeholder implementation\n  # You would need to implement the actual pathfinding logic here\n  actions = []\n  reward = 0.0\n\n  # If primitive is a tool that can be used to get other items (e.g., BRIDGE for WATER, PICKAXE for GEM)\n  if primitive == \"BRIDGE\":\n      # Check if there's water nearby and we can place the bridge\n      if state.next_to(env.world.water_index):\n          actions.extend([env.action_specs()['USE']])\n  elif primitive == \"PICKAXE\":\n      # Check if there's gem nearby and we can mine it\n      if state.next_to(env.world.stone_index):\n          actions.extend([env.action_specs()['USE']])\n\n  # For other primitives, you would need to implement pathfinding logic to reach them\n  # This is a simplified example - you'd want to use A* or similar for actual implementation\n\n  return state, reward, actions", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
