{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T15:14:42.159895", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Find the index of the primitive\n  index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # Check if we already have this primitive in our inventory\n  if state.inventory[index] > 0:\n      return state, reward, []\n  \n  # Use BFS to find the shortest path to collect the primitive\n  queue = collections.deque([(state, [])])\n  visited = set()\n  \n  while queue:\n      current_state, actions = queue.popleft()\n      \n      # Check if we already have the primitive\n      if current_state.inventory[index] > 0:\n          return current_state, reward, actions\n      \n      # Generate next states for all possible actions\n      for action in range(5):  # 5 actions: UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT, USE\n          new_state = current_state.step(action)\n          \n          # Skip if state is invalid or already visited\n          if new_state is None or str(new_state) in visited:\n              continue\n          \n          # Add to queue for exploration\n          queue.append((new_state, actions + [action]))\n          visited.add(str(new_state))\n  \n  return state, reward, []", "island_id": 0, "scores": {"3": -1}}
