{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T15:23:18.437408", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Get the index for the primitive\n  idx = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n  \n  # If we already have it, return empty list\n  if state.inventory[idx] > 0:\n      return [], 0.0, []\n\n  # If we can see it nearby, go get it\n  if state.next_to(idx):\n      # Find where it is and move toward it\n      for dx in range(-1, 2):\n          for dy in range(-1, 2):\n              x = state.pos[0] + dx\n              y = state.pos[1] + dy\n              if (0 <= x < env.world.WIDTH and 0 <= y < env.world.HEIGHT and \n                  env.state.grid[x][y][idx] > 0):\n                  # Move towards this position\n                  if dx == -1:\n                      action_list.append(2)  # LEFT\n                  elif dx == 1:\n                      action_list.append(3)  # RIGHT\n                  elif dy == -1:\n                      action_list.append(0)  # UP\n                  elif dy == 1:\n                      action_list.append(1)  # DOWN\n\n  # Otherwise, try to find a way to reach it using existing tools\n  if not action_list:\n      # Try to use any available tool that might help us access the primitive\n      for item_name in ['BRIDGE', 'PICKAXE']:\n          if item_name in env.world.cookbook.index.contents:\n              item_idx = env.world.cookbook.index[item_name]\n              if state.inventory[item_idx] > 0:\n                  # Try to build or use this tool\n                  # (this would require more complex logic)\n                  pass\n\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 6, "scores": {"3": -1}}
