{"timestamp": "2025-08-15T15:27:02.867628", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Get the index of the primitive from the environment's cookbook\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Check if we already have this primitive in inventory\n  if state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return [], 0, []\n\n  # If not in inventory, find a way to get it.\n  # This is a simplified version that just moves around until it finds the primitive.\n  # A full implementation would require pathfinding and potentially using tools.\n\n  action_list = []\n  reward = 0\n  state = env._current_state\n\n  # Get the index of the primitive from the environment's cookbook\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Check if we already have this primitive in inventory\n  if state.inventory[primitive_index] > 0:\n      return [], 0, []\n\n  # If not in inventory, find a way to get it.\n  # This is a simplified version that just moves around until it finds the primitive.\n  # A full implementation would require pathfinding and potentially using tools.\n\n  # Simple strategy: move towards the primitive if possible\n  # In practice, this should use a proper pathfinder\n\n  for a in action_list:\n      r, state = env.step(state, a)\n      reward += r\n\n  return state, reward, action_list", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
